course: dictionary
lesson: 5041
title: Old-fashioned words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name things we hardly use any more. An inkstand is one of them. It is a stand or tray on a desk that holds pots of ink, pens and sometimes sand or a pen-wiper. In «Never!» says the Queen, throwing an inkstand at the Lizard, the context tells you it is an object on a desk that someone can throw.
explain: Look at the two parts of the word. Ink is the liquid we write with, and a stand is something that holds things up. Put them together and an inkstand holds ink. The desk, the pens and the ink in the story all point the same way.
explain: The context also tells you about time. People used inkstands in the days of dip pens, when you dipped a pen into ink again and again. So an inkstand suggests an old-fashioned desk or office. Most people today write with ballpoint pens, so you rarely see one.
fact: An inkstand is a stand or tray on a desk that holds ink pots and pens.
fact: Some inkstands also held sand or a pen-wiper.
fact: Inkstands were used in the days of dip pens.
fact: «Inkstand» is a noun, so you can say an inkstand or some inkstands.
fact: In «Alice in Wonderland», the Queen throws an inkstand at Bill the Lizard, and the ink trickles down his face.
exercise: In «Alice in Wonderland», what does the Queen throw at Bill the Lizard? | A ballpoint pen | A cup of tea | *An inkstand | A lamp
exercise: What is an inkstand? | A kind of bridge over a river | A bag for carrying books | A small horse from long ago | *A stand or tray on a desk that holds ink pots and pens
exercise: «The old office had an inkstand, pens and a pot of ink on every desk.» What does inkstand suggest about the office? | *It was an old-fashioned office | It was a space station | It had no desks at all | It was a modern café
test: Which clue inside the word inkstand helps you guess its meaning? | It starts with the letter i | It has eight letters | *Ink and stand: it is a stand that holds ink | It is a kind of sport
test: Why would someone in the days of dip pens need an inkstand? | To sit on while writing | To cut paper into shapes | To keep the room warm | *To hold the ink they dipped their pen into
exam: Which fact about an inkstand is true? | It is a kind of animal | It is a type of computer | It is a meal served at tea time | *It was used in the days of dip pens
